[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2776971876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104948#issuecomment-2776971876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104948","id":2776971876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lhTpk","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T21:37:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T21:37:56Z","body":"It feels like an effort has been made to document every time negative indexes are supported. For methods that support them, but do not explicitly mention this, it absolutely should be.\nThe current description is fine, personally. There's nothing inherently misleading about it. I guess one could lightly mention that `slice` should not be negative, but not necessarily because negative indices are supported everywhere else.\n\nThere should _probably_ be an error when the index is negative, yes.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2776971876/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777100735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104948#issuecomment-2777100735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104948","id":2777100735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lhzG_","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T22:07:15Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T22:07:15Z","body":"`get_slice` is a prime example of a method that *shouldn't* support negative indexing for performance reasons, it doesn't know how many slices there are to avoid doing excessive checking\n\nWe *could* make it work backwards with `rfind` but that's a lot of extra code for a very edge case scenario\n\nBut I agree that negative indices should not be assumed to be the default, adding an error here would arguably break compatibility though","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777100735/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2927101040","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104948#issuecomment-2927101040","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104948","id":2927101040,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ueARw","user":{"login":"fcolecumberri","id":12193875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTkzODc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12193875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri","html_url":"https://github.com/fcolecumberri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcolecumberri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-01T11:49:39Z","updated_at":"2025-06-01T11:49:39Z","body":"I understand that tracking a string backwards may be more expensive than tracking forward (If someone does not understand why, check how UTF-8 works).\n\nHowever:\n- in most cases where the slice is positive, the only overhead would be an `if(0<slice)`.\n- and when slice needs to be negative, the alternative is manually tracking backwards anyway.\n\nSo I am not sure if performance is really an issue for supporting negatives in `slice`.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2927101040/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]